LICENCE FOR PARKING AND GEOGRAPHIC DATA

Last updated: March 30, 2026

Please read this Licence carefully before using any parking zone data, geographic data, or related informational datasets provided in this project (hereinafter: “Data”).

By accessing or using the Data, you confirm that you have read, understood, and agreed to this Licence. If you do not agree with any part of this Licence, do not use the Data.

1. Informational Nature of Parking Zone Data

All information about parking zones, including their location, boundaries, pricing, hours of operation, and corresponding service identifiers found in the Data, is for informational purposes only.

In the event of any discrepancies between the Data and the official data from the relevant parking authorities, only the official data from those authorities shall apply.

Users are responsible for verifying parking zone information on official traffic signs posted in the zone where the vehicle is parked. The Data does not guarantee complete accuracy or up-to-date information.

2. Data Accuracy

Efforts are made to provide the most accurate and up-to-date information about parking zones and related geographic data. However, complete accuracy and currency cannot be guaranteed, as updates depend on timely notifications from the relevant authorities and parking service providers, who often do not update their public platforms promptly.

3. Changes to Settlements and Areas

The list of cities, settlements, and areas covered by the Data may change at any time, without prior explicit notice.

It is important to note that the Data is in no way affiliated, partnered, officially supported, or sponsored by any parking service, government authority, or other legal entity.

4. Prohibition on Unauthorized Use and Data Copying

All Data provided herein—including, but not limited to, information about parking zones, their locations, boundaries, prices, hours of operation, and related geographic datasets—is the intellectual property of the Data’s development team. This Data is the result of extensive fieldwork, data collection from users, and the analysis of public sources.

It is strictly forbidden to download, copy ("scrape"), reproduce, distribute, or otherwise use any Data for any commercial or non-commercial purpose without the express prior written consent of the development team. Any breach of this clause will be deemed a copyright infringement and will be subject to legal action under the governing laws.

5. Disclaimer of Warranties

The Data is provided “as is” and “as available,” without any warranties, express or implied, including but not limited to warranties of accuracy, reliability, availability, or fitness for a particular purpose.

6. Limitation of Liability

To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, the development team shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages (including, but not limited to, damages arising from reliance on inaccurate parking or geographic information, loss of profits, data, usage, goodwill, or other intangible losses) resulting from or in any way connected with the use or inability to use the Data, even if the development team has been informed of the possibility of such damages.

7. Languages and Governing Version

This Licence may be available in other languages. However, in the event of any discrepancies or differences in interpretation between language versions, the Serbian version shall be authoritative and shall prevail.

